<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Berzacks raises yr shr, offers scrip div.</title>
<headline>Berzacks raises yr shr, offers scrip div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>		     (million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     146.7	 vs 120.4</p>
<p>    Headline shr (cts)    137.3	 vs 116.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  35.0	 vs  33.5</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    40.09	vs  32.27</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    42.59	vs  33.44</p>
<p>    Tax			   2.46	vs   2.14</p>
<p>    Interest paid	     2.30	vs   4.67</p>
<p>    Turnover		  122.85	vs 130.58</p>
<p>Div payable Dec 4</p>
<p>on register Oct 18</p>
<p>Full name: Berzack Brothers Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	 2.56	vs 1.15</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it had decided to award capitalisation shares to shareholders on register October 18 in the ratio of 1.67 capitalisation shares for every 100 ordinary shares held.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
